<===> README.md
An `@extend` within a media query that can't be unified with the target
(e.g. two different ids) extends nothing, so like in dart-sass it's no error
that the target is outside of that media query.
<===>
================================================================================
<===> elements_dont_unify/input.scss
a.t {a: b}
@media screen {b {@extend .t}}
<===> elements_dont_unify/output.css
a.t {
  a: b;
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> ids_dont_unify/input.scss
#y.t {a: b}
@media screen {#x {@extend .t}}
<===> ids_dont_unify/output.css
#y.t {
  a: b;
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> same_media/input.scss
@media screen {.t {a: b} .x {@extend .t}}
<===> same_media/output.css
@media screen {
  .t, .x {
    a: b;
  }
}
